  S4 -- the cosmological ordering (does not need overlap):
    alt: cluster outskirts  rho_b = 4.42e-25 kg/m^3, Phi_loc = 2.75e+11 m^2/s^2, g_bar = 8.93e-12 m/s^2, E = 1.68
           cosmic background  rho_b = 4.18e-28 kg/m^3 (1057x LOWER), Phi_loc -> 0, g_bar -> 0 (homogeneous)
    canonical: cluster outskirts  rho_b = 4.42e-25 kg/m^3, Phi_loc = 2.75e+11 m^2/s^2, g_bar = 8.93e-12 m/s^2, E = 1.82
           cosmic background  rho_b = 4.18e-28 kg/m^3 (1057x LOWER), Phi_loc -> 0, g_bar -> 0 (homogeneous)
    => a monotone S(X) that unscreens clusters relative to galaxies unscreens the BACKGROUND at least as much,
       so G_cosmo/G_local >= E(cluster outskirts) = 1.82; BBN allows |G/G_0 - 1| < 0.2, i.e. 4x the bound.
  [FAIL] S4 [cosmology] the homogeneous background is NOT beyond cluster outskirts in every candidate variable, so monotone screening can decouple G_cosmo from G_cluster   (it is beyond in all of them (density 1057x lower, potential and acceleration -> 0), forcing G_cosmo/G_local >= 1.82)
  [FAIL] S5 [verdict] the screened-force route survives the overlap tests AND the cosmological ordering   (the ordering argument is independent of which variable is screened and of whether the populations overlap)

  what remains open, stated rather than closed: (i) a TIME-dependent transition (a field that rolls late) evades the
  ordering argument because the background value at BBN and today differ -- that is not screening, it is a cosmological
  history, and it must then face the CMB and growth of structure; (ii) a non-monotone S, or S of two variables at once,
  is a fitted function rather than a screening mechanism.  Neither is claimed closed here.

RESULT: 5 FAIL -> ['S1 [potential] clusters and galaxies at the same potential depth require the SAME enhancement, so a potential-screened force is admissible', 'S2 [density] clusters and galaxies at the same baryon density require the SAME enhancement, so a density-screened force is admissible', 'S3 [mass] clusters and galaxies at the same enclosed baryonic mass require the SAME enhancement, so a mass-screened force is admissible', 'S4 [cosmology] the homogeneous background is NOT beyond cluster outskirts in every candidate variable, so monotone screening can decouple G_cosmo from G_cluster', 'S5 [verdict] the screened-force route survives the overlap tests AND the cosmological ordering']
